Rook to the open c or d-file. Which to choose?  Best is "
OK

MOVE Rc1
"1.Rc1! "
OK

"grabbing the c-file. Now after"
OK

MOVE Rd8
"1...Rd8?!"
OK

"(I put this sign ?! to denote the meaning 'dubious move'. When you see this 
sign, it means that the player has a better choice of moves.), grabbing the 
d-file, White plays"
OK

MOVE Kf1
"2.Kf1, preparing to penetrate Black's position with his Rook. Black plays"
OK

MOVE Kf8
"2...Kf8, returning the favor. White now plays"
OK

MOVE Rc7
"3.Rc7, penetrating Black's camp. Now"
OK

MOVE Rd2
"3...Rd2 can be met by "
OK

MOVE Rxb7
"4.Rxb7, winning a pawn and eventually the game."
OK

DIAGRAM "a2,b2,e3,f2,g2,h2,Rf1,Kg1 v a7,b7,e6,f7,g7,h7,Rf8,Kg8" WHITE
