OK

DIAGRAM "a5,b4,c5,e3,f2,g3,Be1,Kf1 v a6,b5,e5,e4,g4,h6,Nd5,Kd3" WHITE
MOVELIST "c6 Nc7 Kg1 Ne6 Kf1 h5 Kg2 Kc4 Kf1 Kd5 Ke2 Kxc6"
"Losing a tempo so that White has to move. If he moves his King, with 
16.Kg1 Ke2 wins the White Bishop."
OK

"White is forced to give up his beautiful passed pawn and Black wraps up 
the game.  17.c6 Nc7 18.Kg1 Ne6 19.Kf1 h5 20.Kg2 Kc4 21.Kf1 Kd5 22.Ke2 Kxc6"
OK

DIAGRAM "a5,b4,e3,f2,g3,Be1,Ke2 v a6,b5,e5,e4,g4,h5,Ne6,Kc6"  WHITE
"Black has realized his objective. He has won White's protected passed pawn, 
but his doubled e-pawns don't offer a passed pawn of his own."
OK

"To win the game, Black has to go back to the c4-square with his King. 
That means coordinating with the Knight to force White's King back."
OK

"23.Kd2!"
MOVE Kd2
OK

DIAGRAM "a5,b4,e3,f2,g3,Be1,Kd2 v a6,b5,e5,e4,g4,h5,Ne6,Kc6" BLACK
MOVELIST "Ng5 Kc2 Kd5 Kb3 Nf3 Bc3 h4"
